                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b8a947df-1c34-3f4b-9cc0-2b8e24c359e9",
                        "entry_id": "15461f86-6f33-32ea-9bef-bcf1fa61fbf1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Resembling or characteristic of a sewer."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8841abc8-bb34-49da-a1fe-d80f6a12a512",
                                "sense_id": "b8a947df-1c34-3f4b-9cc0-2b8e24c359e9",
                                "text": "Also how he saw a “brooke,” which was doubtless in his time a pretty little river, but which is now a sewery looking stream that tries to atone for its shallowness and narrowness by its thickness."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0cc543a9-2e5d-4a67-a68b-5cfa063797b1",
                                "sense_id": "b8a947df-1c34-3f4b-9cc0-2b8e24c359e9",
                                "text": "The litter-strewn mud when the tide was out somehow offended them much less than the sewery water when it was up."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "93af304d-1728-4271-9719-cb54a603afb1",
                                "sense_id": "b8a947df-1c34-3f4b-9cc0-2b8e24c359e9",
                                "text": "Once King James risked the crown on a voyage beneath the sewery river."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "23f2a960-30b5-47e5-b596-490047db5bd0",
                                "sense_id": "b8a947df-1c34-3f4b-9cc0-2b8e24c359e9",
                                "text": "He woke outside on the grass, on his stomach, his nostrils filled with an acid, sewery smell, and something was on top of him, crushing him, being lifted off for a second, then crushing him again."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e20ff2e-ccbd-4647-90c0-08bc36eacc2a",
                                "sense_id": "b8a947df-1c34-3f4b-9cc0-2b8e24c359e9",
                                "text": "“These aren’t sewer-pipes, anyway,” Stan said from behind them. “You can tell by that smell. It’s bad, but it’s not a sewery smell.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6404c25d-7144-4d39-9e47-6e364cb806af",
                                "sense_id": "b8a947df-1c34-3f4b-9cc0-2b8e24c359e9",
                                "text": "I will only add here one word of advice to my readers: never tolerate a sewery smell in any part of your house: you know not to what it may lead."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c7d1266e-647a-49be-bfa3-d61f559c4c6e",
                                "sense_id": "b8a947df-1c34-3f4b-9cc0-2b8e24c359e9",
                                "text": "Grandma’s was crowded and smelled of potpourri sachets and Christmassy dusting powder and the faint sewery smell from the bathroom it led to."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
